<!--
  Better Crossbreeding (DizzyEevee.BetterCrossbreeding, Workshop 3520675842).

  HOW THE TWO HALVES WORK. Which animals may mate is decided by vanilla, and by the MALE only:
  JobGiver_Mate looks for a fertile female of the male's own def, then of each def in the male's own
  <race><canCrossBreedWith>. What is born is decided by the mod: it reads a DZY.CrossBreeding.Extension on
  the MOTHER's PawnKindDef, whose <outcomes> are keyed by the father's kind (Maternal, Paternal, Random,
  or Other with weighted children). A mother without the extension keeps the vanilla result, her own kind.
  So a pair needs the list on the male's race AND the extension on the mother's kind, in both directions,
  for both parents to be able to sire.

  THE CLASS NAME. The mod's own Example/Patches/Example.xml writes Class="DZY.Crossbreeding.Extension",
  with a lower-case b. The compiled assembly declares DZY.CrossBreeding.Extension, capital B. This file uses
  the assembly's spelling; a patch copied from the Example would name a type that does not exist.

  WHAT THIS FILE DECIDES. The four animals whose own text says they are a member of a vanilla species,
  the same four pairs as DogsMatePatch.xml (the reasons for each, and for the animals left out, are there):

    MM_Cerberus <-> Husky, LabradorRetriever, YorkshireTerrier
    MM_ErymanthianBoar <-> WildBoar, Pig
    MM_CeryneianHind <-> Deer, Elk, Caribou
    MM_Pegasus <-> Horse

  The calf is either parent's kind on a coin flip (Random), as for any two races of one species.
  Every pair has one animal of this mod: a pairing between two vanilla animals belongs to Animal
  Naturally, not here (owner's rule of 2026-09-28).

  A vanilla animal is patched only to add its new partner. Each list is created if the race has none, and
  appended to if another mod already made one: a plain Add on <race> would write a second
  <canCrossBreedWith> and silently replace the first. The extension is created only when the kind does not
  carry one already, for the same reason.

  Everything sits inside one PatchOperationFindMod on the mod's display name, so without Better
  Crossbreeding this file changes nothing and logs nothing. No load order: the extension is an XML node
  parsed after every assembly is loaded.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
